# PROJECT PROMPT: FUTURISTIC FASHION BRAND PORTFOLIO & INTERACTIVE LOOKBOOK

## 1. Your Role

Act as a world-class fashion art director, creative director, senior UI/UX designer, motion designer, and expert frontend developer.

Your task is to design and build a complete, visually exceptional, modern, responsive, and interactive fashion brand portfolio website inspired by the futuristic web design reference below.

**Figma design reference:**
https://www.figma.com/community/file/1510588455428094314/how-to-create-futuristic-website-ui-in-figma-ux-design-tutorial?q_id=65cf443b-f642-4ee8-9110-a630b2f093f3

First, inspect the reference design if access is available. Study its layout, visual hierarchy, typography, color palette, navigation, image composition, futuristic elements, transitions, and interaction patterns.

Translate its design principles into a premium fashion portfolio and lookbook experience. Do not blindly reproduce a generic template. Adapt the design to the unique visual storytelling needs of fashion designers, independent fashion labels, fashion stylists, creative studios, and heritage fashion houses.

If the reference cannot be accessed, do not pretend to have inspected it. Use the futuristic editorial art direction described in this prompt and continue building.

## 2. Project Overview

Create a fashion brand portfolio and digital lookbook platform that allows a fashion brand to present its identity, collections, campaigns, creative process, and artistic philosophy through an immersive website.

This is primarily a **brand presentation and visual storytelling platform, not an e-commerce store**.

The main goals are to:

- Showcase fashion collections through immersive photography and editorial layouts.
- Communicate the brand's identity, philosophy, and design language.
- Present seasonal collections and curated lookbooks.
- Highlight individual outfits, styling concepts, fabrics, silhouettes, and details.
- Tell the story behind each collection.
- Attract fashion editors, models, photographers, stylists, buyers, collaborators, and potential clients.
- Make it easy for visitors to explore collections and contact the brand.
- Establish a distinctive, memorable digital brand identity.

The finished website should feel like an award-winning experimental fashion website created by a high-end creative studio.

