## 12. Performance, Accessibility, and SEO

Performance:
- Optimize image delivery.
- Lazy-load below-the-fold media.
- Avoid unnecessarily large JavaScript bundles.
- Prevent layout shifts by specifying image dimensions or aspect ratios.
- Minimize excessive animation.
- Avoid loading all full-resolution gallery images immediately.

Accessibility:
- Use semantic landmarks.
- Ensure sufficient text contrast.
- Support keyboard navigation.
- Provide visible focus indicators.
- Label form fields.
- Use descriptive image alt text.
- Support reduced motion.
- Make overlays and mobile navigation accessible.

SEO:
- Provide unique page titles and meta descriptions.
- Add Open Graph metadata.
- Use meaningful page URLs.
- Include a favicon and brand identity.
- Add canonical URLs when appropriate.
- Generate a sitemap and robots.txt for production deployment.
- Use appropriate structured data only when it accurately describes the brand or content.

